# Rate Card Service - Project Structure Guide

This is a Go microservice for rate card management following clean architecture principles with factory pattern for handling multiple rate providers (static and dynamic).

## Directory Structure Overview

### Entry Points
- [cmd/server/main.go](mdc:cmd/server/main.go) - Main application entry point
- [cmd/test/main.go](mdc:cmd/test/main.go) - Test runner entry point

### API Documentation
- [api_docs/architecture/](mdc:api_docs/architecture) - Design documents and architecture decisions
- [api_docs/openapi/v1/](mdc:api_docs/openapi/v1) - REST API specifications
- [api_docs/proto/v1/](mdc:api_docs/proto/v1) - gRPC protocol buffer definitions

### Infrastructure Layer
- [internal/infrastructure/api/grpc/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/grpc) - gRPC server setup and configuration
- [internal/infrastructure/api/grpc/interceptors/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/grpc/interceptors) - Authentication, logging, and other interceptors
- [internal/infrastructure/api/grpc/v1/handlers/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/grpc/v1/handlers) - gRPC request handlers
- [internal/infrastructure/api/http/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/http) - HTTP server setup and configuration
- [internal/infrastructure/api/http/middleware/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/http/middleware) - Global HTTP middleware
- [internal/infrastructure/api/http/v1/handlers/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/http/v1/handlers) - HTTP request handlers
- [internal/infrastructure/api/http/v1/routes/](mdc:internal/infrastructure/api/http/v1/routes) - Route definitions

